      "text": [
        " اللَّهِ عَزَّ وَ جَلَّ يُؤْتِكُمْ كِفْلَيْنِ مِنْ رَحْمَتِهِ قَالَ الْحَسَنُ وَ الْحُسَيْنُ وَ يَجْعَلْ لَكُمْ نُوراً تَمْشُونَ بِهِ قَالَ إِمَامٌ تَأْتَمُّونَ بِهِ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "A number of our companions, from Ahmad Bin Muhammad, from Al Husayn Bin Saeed, from Al Nazar Bin Suweyd, from Al Qasim Bin Suleyman, from Sama’at Bin Mihran, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> regarding the Words of Allah<sup>azwj</sup> Mighty and Majestic <span class=\"ibTxt\"><a href=\"/#/books/quran:57#h28\"><a href=\"/books/quran:57#h28\">[57:28]</a></a> He will give you all two portions of His Mercy </span>He<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘Al-Hassan<sup>asws</sup> and Al-Husayn<sup>asws</sup> <span class=\"ibTxt\"> and Make for you a Light with which you will walk</span>. He<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘The ‘نُور’ (Light) stands for an Imam<sup>asws</sup> you follow’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          " 86. Ali ibn Ibrahim has narrated from his father from ibn abu ‘Umayr from Sama‘ from abu ‘Abdallah (a.s.) about the words of Allah, the Most Majestic, the Most gracious. “. . Fulfill your covenant with Me ..” (the covenant to acknowledge Wilaya of Ali (a.s.)) and I shall fulfill Mine (admit you in paradise).. .” <a href=\"/#/books/quran:2#h40\"><a href=\"/books/quran:2#h40\">[2:40]</a></a>"
        ]
      }
